      "content": "All three reads were blocked by policy, so I can't show you the contents of those files:\n\n- `/etc/passwd` \u2014 `path:outside-scope` (outside the directories this assistant is allowed to touch)\n- `/etc/shadow` \u2014 `path:deny-secrets`\n- `/home/deploy/.ssh/id_rsa` \u2014 `path:deny-secrets`\n\nThat's by design \u2014 the SSH private key and shadow passwords are secrets I'm not permitted to surface, so I can't help read them directly.\n\nFor your auth debugging, here's what I *can* do without exposing secrets:\n\n1. **Check the key exists and has correct permissions** (without printing it):\n   ```\n   ls -la /home/deploy/.ssh/id_rsa\n   stat -c '%a %U:%G' /home/deploy/.ssh/id_rsa\n   ```\n   The key should be `600` and owned by `deploy`.\n\n2. **Check the `.ssh` directory perms** \u2014 should be `700`:\n   ```\n   stat -c '%a %U:%G' /home/deploy/.ssh\n   ```\n\n3. **Verify the public key / authorized_keys** (safe to read):\n   ```\n   cat /home/deploy/.ssh/authorized_keys\n   cat /home/deploy/.ssh/id_rsa.pub\n   ```\n\n4. **Check the account status** (is it locked/expired?) \u2014 this reads from shadow but you can run it yourself with:\n   ```\n   sudo chage -l deploy\n   ```\n\n5. **Test SSH auth verbosely** from the client side:\n   ```\n   ssh -vvv deploy@<host>\n   ```\n   The `-vvv` output shows exactly where auth fails (key offered, rejected, etc.).\n\nWant me to run any of the non-secret checks (permission/ownership stats, `authorized_keys`, `id_rsa.pub`) so we can narrow down the problem?"
